  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Crowdfunding Subsidy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While both Somali and Somaliland have a formal government, it is relatively small and has very limited legislation for financial transactions. The private financial sector is dominated by some powerful factions and takes the lead in economic development in a way that benefits their interests. For SME&#x2019;s that do not fit into this, it is very difficult to obtain loans for investments. Most depend on their own networks and for those without the proper affiliations it is next to impossible to find investors. African Crowdfunding (ACF) will use crowdfunding as an alternative option for Somali diaspora to contribute to the growth of small businesses in a transparent, inclusive and sustainable manner. African Crowdfunding should test and finetune its&#x2019; proposition, before being able to stand on its&#x2019; own feet and successfully and for the longer term become a source of SME funding for Somali entrepreneurs. External funding to support African Crowdfunding in its&#x2019; first 30 months of operation, could accelerate this process considerably and increase the chances of being successful.</narrative>
  </description>
